  "preamble": "Fronting of the voiceless uvular stop [q] to an aspirated velar stop [kʰ] moves the closure from the uvula to the soft palate and adds aspiration. Pittayaporn (2009) reconstructs a Proto-Tai uvular *q that merged with *x and *χ as kʰ (spelled ข) in Southwestern Tai, while Northern Tai Zhuang keeps the series apart (*q > k, *χ > h).",
